      "id": "fst-wounded",
      "type": "adventure",
      "x": 7100,
      "speaker": "Wounded Man",
      "lines": [
        "Don't — don't come closer with a blade out.",
        "Boar caught me at the ford. Can't put weight on it and the light's going.",
        "I'm no use to you like this. But I've carried a shield in a line before, and I'd carry one again for whoever gets me upright."
      ],
      "choices": [
        "Bind the leg and stay till dawn",
        "Leave him your water and go on"
      ],
      "responses": [
        "It costs you a night and most of your strength. By morning he can stand. Corran, he says, and takes his place on your left where the shield does the most good.",
        "He takes it with both hands. It is not enough and you both know it."
      ],
      "outcomes": [
